I used to have Hack 1.03 running on 8088 and while other kids were playing
arcade games on their C-64's, I was attempting to fetch the Amulet of Yendor...
they all thought the game must suck, but little did they know.  Yeah, 1.03 was
a hit or miss game at best... no matter how carefully you played, you could
still get wasted in a single turn.  I've played nethack for so long its hard to
remember the old one.  It wasn't possible to ascend (that didn't come till
3.0), so the point was to grab the amulet and head to the surface.  The only
way was to get teleportation, teleport control, fire resistance, and find a 
level teleporter since there were no stairs to hell.  Woe to the adventurer who
hit a level teleporter w/o t-control... more often than not he was sent
straight to heaven or hell (occasionally sent to a spot a few hundred feet
above dungeon level one -- nasty fall).  One tin of spinach could improve your
strength from 15 to 18/** and there was no prompt asking you whether you wanted
to stop eating or not.  Robbing shops was easy... just eat one of the many
leprechauns you encounter and teleport out.  The shopkeeper just followed you
around asking for payment... there was no use for money (i once gathered over
100000 zorkmids from dungeon levels).  There were many bugs:  zapping a wand of
polymorph or a wand of nothing would sometimes lock the keyboard, as would
eating mimics.  The best bug was in the code for the trapper (monster)... the
trapper increased your hit points instead of decreased... i managed to get my
character up to about 6000 hit points before i got bored.  The killer bees were
by far the worst monsters and cavemen were the best characters.  The WoY might
as well not have existed in the game for all the danger he posed my character. 
I got so I could win the game fairly frequently.  Not so with 3.1.3  :(
Hmmmm.... mebbe i still have 1.03 somewhere  :)

